 3600 6-Core Processor (12 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nWith Autowrap mode set to Word (or Word (Smart)), when a line is supposed to break in the middle of a Thai word that contains upper/lower vowels or tone marks, it displays the consonant with those characters twice, one each before and after the line break. However, in some specific cases, instead of displaying a few characters twice, an entire word is not displayed at all.\n\nBelow is an example of incorrectly displayed line breaks. The spaces before the text have no effects on the broken line breaks.\nThe Correct column is me manually adding line breaks to show what it should've look like.\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0315c357-3e3b-4ae6-a698-4801cd8c15b8)\n\nHere are the problematic characters:\n(Taken from https://jrgraphix.net/r/Unicode/0E00-0E7F)\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/82083f26-c05b-47df-b493-297d670b02a7)\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Add a Label\n- Set Autowrap mode to Word\n- Set text to \"             กู้ไฟล์\"\n- Adjust Label size until a line break occurs at the word \"กู้\"\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nProject containing the table in the screenshot: [ThaiAutowrapBug.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/17833870/ThaiAutowrapBug.zip)\n","closed_by":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs",